{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments ["<b>And the curse, if you do not hear.</b> Meaning: one who withholds himself from hearing the Torah — behold, he is cursed on his own. And this is the reading of the verse, ״וְהַקְּלָלָה אִם לֹא תִשְׁמְעוּ״ — this itself is the curse. Furthermore, [the curse] will pursue him to turn aside from the totality of the path of life, as He concludes saying, <b>and you turn aside from the path</b>, etc. And not only that, but it will hew for him broken cisterns, as it says, <b>to go after</b>, etc."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:16:40.669897057Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}